each bill's amount and due date.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A sent email to the AP lead listing all unpaid bills with 
vendor/invoice identifiers, amounts, and due dates, plus confirmation with the 
sent-message reference and a cross-check showing the list matches ERP read-only 
data.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Use the ERP read-only API to discover and verify bill data; do not create, 
edit, or delete bills, vendors, or payments.
  - Send exactly one email for this request, only to the identified AP lead 
recipient.
  - Include every unpaid bill in the ERP as of 2026-10-11; exclude bills that 
are fully paid.
  - Do not guess missing amounts, due dates, statuses, or recipient addresses; 
if required data cannot be determined, stop and report the blocker instead of 
sending an incomplete or incorrect email.
  - Use the AP shared mailbox as the sending account unless company systems 
identify a different required sender for this request.
  - Any approval required by policy for sending the email is approval-gated by 
the platform; do not treat approval as a separate manual subgoal.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. The AP shared mailbox Sent folder contains exactly one new email sent 
during this run to the AP lead address, and that email lists every unpaid bill 
in the ERP as of 2026-10-11 with its amount and due date.
  C2. Every bill included in the email is unpaid in the ERP as of 2026-10-11, 
and no fully paid bill is included.
  C3. No ERP records were created or modified, and no payment was scheduled or 
made.
  C4. The email recipient address corresponds to the AP lead as evidenced by 
company systems or mailbox records, and no unintended recipients were included.
  C5. If the AP lead recipient cannot be reliably determined, or the unpaid-bill
list cannot be reliably compiled, no email is sent and the blocker is reported 
with supporting evidence.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The AP lead's email address is discoverable from the AP shared mailbox or 
company records; if it is not, the run stops rather than guessing a recipient.
  - The email should be sent from the available AP shared mailbox account.
  - Unpaid means not fully paid as of 2026-10-11; partially paid bills, if any, 
are treated according to the default assumption above.
  - Amounts and due dates are taken directly from the ERP bill records without 
modification.
  - The list can be organized by due date or vendor for readability, but all 
unpaid bills must be included.
PLAN:
  S1: Retrieve all relevant bills from the ERP using read-only APIs and 
determine which are unpaid as of 2026-10-11. (done when: A complete, 
deduplicated set of unpaid bill records with amount and due date is extracted, 
and any ambiguity in unpaid status is resolved or explicitly flagged.)
  S2: Identify the AP lead's email address from the AP shared mailbox or other 
company systems. (done when: A single recipient address is identified with 
evidence linking it to the AP lead role, or a blocker is recorded if no reliable
address exists.)
  S3: Compose the email to the AP lead containing the complete unpaid-bill list 
with amounts and due dates, including helpful identifiers such as vendor and 
invoice number. (done when: A draft exists in the mail compose page addressed to
the identified AP lead and containing every unpaid bill from S1 exactly once.)
  S4: Send the email to the AP lead. (done when: The message appears in the Sent
folder with a sent timestamp and the correct recipient.)
  S5: Verify the sent email against ERP read-only data and confirm no unintended
changes occurred. (done when: A cross-check shows all unpaid bills are present, 
no paid bills are present, and no ERP records or extra emails were created or 
modified.)
